# The accounts under screen time talk to the root daemon through this one
# command, and only this one: answering a math problem, or a grown-up typing
# their password in the bar to hand out minutes, has no terminal to carry a
# sudo prompt. Membership comes with `omarchy-screen-time-admin add`. The
# command reads the password from stdin, acts only on the account sudo says is
# calling, and checks every argument itself; sudoers passes the arguments
# through because the shapes (a minute count, a question id) are the command's
# to validate, not a pattern's.
%omarchy-screen-time ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/omarchy-screen-time-ctl
